"Listen in the car (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-in-the-car?nocache=https%3A%2F%2Fhelp.audible.com%2Fs%2Farticle%2Flisten-in-the-car%3Flanguage%3Den_US)\nciteturn763search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: last month; You won't be able to use Apple CarPlay or Android Auto with this connection, but you can play titles directly from the Audible app on your phone with the option to use Car Mode. ...   * Alexa tap to talk ... If you sign in to Audible with a username, please contact the Audible Customer Service team to get help.\n\n## Listen in the car\n\n  * Oct 24, 2025\n  * Knowledge\n\nTitle\n\nListen in the car\n\nURL Name\n\nlisten-in-the-car\n\nAnswer\n\nAudible is compatible with Android Auto, Android Automotive Operating System, Apple CarPlay, and the Waze app. You can also use Car Mode in the Audible app for a simplified listening experience.\n\nTip: To listen in your car, make sure you're connected to a network to stream titles, or download titles to your Library ahead of time for offline listening.\n\nSafety warning: Do not interact with this app while driving. Use this app only when allowed by law and applicable traffic rules and when it is safe to do so. Using the Audible app while driving is dangerous and may result in serious injury, death, or property damage.\n\n## How do I connect to my car with Bluetooth, USB, or AUX?\n\nYou can listen with the Audible app in your car over Bluetooth, USB, or AUX.\n\nConnect via Bluetooth\n\nYou can listen to the Audible app with Car Mode over Bluetooth. After pairing your device for the first time, it will automatically connect to your car in the future.\n\n  1. In your device Settings, turn Bluetooth on and set your device to \"discoverable.\"\n  2. Activate your car's Bluetooth. These steps may vary depending on your car's system.\n  3. Pair your device with your car. You may be prompted to enter a code.\n\nConnect via USB cable\n\nYou must have a USB port built-in directly to your vehicle's sound system to connect this way.\n\n  1. Check for a USB port in your car.\n  2. Connect your phone with a USB cable.\n\nConnect via AUX cable\n\nAn AUX cable is different from a USB cable. It plugs directly into your radio or car with a headphone jack. You won't be able to use Apple CarPlay or Android Auto with this connection, but you can play titles directly from the Audible app on your phone with the option to use Car Mode.\n\n  1. Check for an AUX port in your car.\n  2. Connect your phone with an AUX cable.\n\n## How do I listen with Android Auto or Apple CarPlay?\n\nWith Android Auto or Apple CarPlay, you can enjoy a simplified listening experience through your car's built-in display and stereo.\n\nNote: You can also use your voice to control Audible on Android Auto with Alexa. Alexa isn't available when using Apple CarPlay, but you can use Siri instead.\n\nListen on your car's display\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Connect your phone via USB to your Android Auto-compatible or CarPlay-compatible stereo.\n  3. If Audible is already playing, it will continue to play through your car stereo. If not, launch the Audible app on your display and pick a title from your Library.\n  4. If you don't see the title you wish to play on your car's display, you can play it from the Audible app on your phone.\n\nNote: CarPlay requires an iPhone 5 or later to use. Some newer cars support CarPlay via Bluetooth. See your owner's manual for more information.\n\n## How do I listen with Android Automotive Operating System?\n\nAndroid Automotive Operating System (AAOS) is built directly into your car — no phone required. You can install the Audible app directly on your car's display.\n\nInstall the app\n\nNote: Installing the Audible app requires an active internet connection.\n\n  1. Open the Google Play Store in your car's display.\n  2. Search for the Audible app.\n  3. Select the Audible app.\n  4. Select Install.\n\nSign in to the Audible app\n\nDepending on your app version, you can sign in by QR code, code, or with email and password.\n\nUse a QR code\n\n  1. Scan the QR code from the Audible app on your car's display using the camera on your phone.\n  2. Follow the on-screen prompts to enter the email and password associated with your Audible account.\n\nUse a code\n\n  1. Select Sign In with code.\n  2. Visit www.amazon.com/code on your mobile device and sign in using your Amazon email and password associated with your Audible account.\n  3. Enter the code found on your car's screen.\n\nNote: If your code isn't working or if you're experiencing any issues entering your code, you can select I need a new code on the car screen to receive an updated code.\n\nUse email and password\n\n  1. Select Sign In with email and password.\n  2. Follow the on-screen prompts to enter the Amazon email and password associated with your Audible account.\n\n## How do I listen in Car Mode?\n\nCar Mode is a feature in the Audible app for both iOS and Android. It provides a simplified listening experience including hands-free voice controls. There are only four buttons on the screen:\n\n  * Alexa tap to talk\n  * Play/Pause\n  * Go Back 30 Seconds\n  * Add a Bookmark\n\nNote: For hands-free listening on the go, you can also use your voice with Alexa or Siri to control Audible. Turn on voice controls and try saying \"Go back 3 minutes.\"\n\nTurn on Car Mode\n\n  1. Open your player in the app.\n  2. Select the Car Mode icon.\n\nTurn off Car Mode\n\n  1. Select the X to exit Car Mode.\n\nTurn on Automatic Car Mode\n\nAutomatic Car Mode is available in the Audible app for iOS and Android. When it's on, Car Mode will launch in your player whenever your phone connects to your car via Bluetooth.\n\nNote: You can also turn this feature off anytime from the same Player settings.\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Select Player.\n  4. Turn on Automatic Car Mode.\n\n## How do I listen with Waze?\n\nThe Audible app for both iOS and Android is compatible with any Waze version 4.69 or higher.\n\nAllow Waze integration in the Audible app\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Select Connect to other apps.\n  4. Toggle on Waze integration.\n\nAllow Audible integration in the Waze app\n\n  1. Open Waze.\n  2. Go to Settings.\n  3. Select Audio player.\n  4. Toggle on Show on the map.\n\nHow to play titles in the Waze app\n\nYou can skip forward and back, play, and pause your Audible titles within the Waze app.\n\n  1. Open Waze.\n  2. Select the Audio player icon.\n  3. Select Audible and allow it to connect to Audible.\n  4. Select Show list to view your 8 most recent titles.\n  5. To listen to other titles, select Open Audible.\n\nNote: If you need additional support using the Waze app, please visit the Waze Help Center.\n\n## How do I listen in my Tesla?\n\nTesla cars now allow you to listen to Audible through your car's built-in display and stereo system via the Audible for Tesla app.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nView listening log (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-listening-log?language=en_US)\nciteturn763search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 2 days ago; The Audible Listen Log is a feature that tracks your listening stats and activity. ... The Listen Log can help you find your place if you get lost. ...   * you accidentally moved the scrubber bar in the player and the book is now in a different section altogether. ... Swipe down to Activity & Stats.\n\n## View listening log\n\nThe Audible Listen Log is a feature that tracks your listening stats and activity. It shows you everything from when you first started a title to when you finished listening to it, including dates and times.\n\n## What is the Listen Log?\n\nYour Listen Log is a day-to-day record of your listening activity for a particular title. You can see the date and time you started listening, when you paused, and how long your listening session lasted.\n\nNotes:\n\n  * The Listen Log displays both dates and times for each session.\n  * Listen Log data cannot be downloaded or exported.\n\n## What is the purpose of the Listen Log?\n\nThe Listen Log can help you find your place if you get lost. It's a very useful tool if, for example:\n\n  * you fell asleep while listening and the book advanced without you;\n  * you went back to an earlier chapter to re-listen to something, but didn't note where you had left off;\n  * you accidentally moved the scrubber bar in the player and the book is now in a different section altogether.\n\nUsing the Listen Log, you can get back to the starting point of your last intentional listening section.\n\n## How do I find my Listen Log?\n\nThe Listen Log is available only on the Audible app and can be accessed through these steps:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Open the player for a title you're currently enjoying or already finished.\n  3. Select the Listen Log button below the cover of the book.\n\nFrom here, you can choose to replay a section or clear your entire history.\n\n## How do I view my Listening History?\n\nYour Listening History shows all the titles you've listened to over time.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Profile.\n  3. Swipe down to Activity & Stats.\n  4. Select Listening History.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listen History.\n\n\n## How do I remove a title from my Listening History?\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listen History.\n  4. Select Remove next to the title you want to remove.\n\nNote: Listening History data cannot be downloaded or exported.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUse timer (https://help.audible.com/s/article/use-timer?nocache=https%3A%2F%2Fhelp.audible.com%2Fs%2Farticle%2Fuse-timer%3Flanguage%3Des_MX)\nciteturn763search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; The Audible timer allows you to control when your audiobook will stop playing so you never lose your place again. ... In this article: ... Select the Timer icon at the bottom of the player or the “countdown banner” on top of the cover of the book ... Swipe to Timer.\n\n## Use timer\n\n  * Sep 3, 2026\n\nAnswer\n\nThe Audible timer allows you to control when your audiobook will stop playing so you never lose your place again.\n\nNote: The timer feature is available only in the Audible app.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * How to set the timer?\n  * How to extend your timer while it's running?\n  * How to extend your timer when it ends?\n  * How to turn on or off your shake-to-extend setting?\n  * How to use the timer with iOS Live Activity?\n\n## How to set the timer?\n\n  1. Open your player while a title is playing.\n  2. Select the Timer icon.\n  3. Choose a preset time or create and save a custom length.\n  4. Once time is up, your audiobook will stop playing.\n\n## How to extend your timer while it's running?\n\nIf you'd like to change the timer while it's still counting down, you can overwrite it with a new time.\n\n  1. Open your player while a title is playing.\n  2. Select the Timer icon at the bottom of the player or the “countdown banner” on top of the cover of the book\n  3. Select a new time from the menu to overwrite the current timer.\n\n## How to extend your timer when it ends?\n\nWhen the timer ends, you'll get an alert. You can choose to extend the timer for the same amount of time or reset it with a new time.\n\nTo extend your timer for the same amount of time, you can shake your phone within 30 seconds of the audio starting to fade.\n\n## How to turn on or off your shake-to-extend setting?\n\nYou can change your timer settings anytime in the app.\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Select Player.\n  4. Swipe to Timer.\n  5. Toggle Shake to extend on or off.\n\n## How to use the timer with iOS Live Activity?\n\niOS Live Activity is automatically turned on for all iPhones with iOS 17.0 or later. Whenever you set your timer, the Timer Live Activity will be visible from your phone's lock screen or dynamic island so you can see the time remaining without opening your iOS device.\n\n  * For all iOS devices, you can shake your phone to extend the timer.\n  * For all iOS devices with iOS 17.0 or later, you can select Live Activity from the lock screen to access your timer.\n  * On all iPhone 14 Pros, you can select Live Activity on Apple's Dynamic Island to access your timer.\n\nNote: You can allow Audible Live Activities for Audible in your device settings. You can also accept or reject Live Activities from the Audible app when you see the Timer Live Activity for the first time.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMissing title issues (https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-is-missing)\nciteturn763search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: today; If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player. ... Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\n## Refresh your Library\n\nYou can refresh your Library by swiping down from the top of the screen until you see the spinning circle. (That means it's refreshing.)\n\nIf a swipe-to-refresh doesn't work, you can do a manual refresh:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Profile.\n  3. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  4. Select Library.\n  5. Select Refresh Library.\n\nNote: If you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh. See the \"Update your app\" section below if refreshing doesn't resolve the issue.\n\n## Check your marketplace\n\nYou may be signed in to the wrong Audible marketplace. If that's the case, none of your titles will be available to listen to. Sign out and then sign in to the Audible marketplace where you made your purchases.\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Profile.\n  3. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  4. Scroll down and select Sign Out twice.\n  5. Select Sign In once and you'll be brought to the welcome screen.\n\n## Check your purchase history on the Audible site\n\nYou can check your recent purchase by going to your Purchase history on the Audible site within your account.\n\nYour default payment method may not have gone through—or you may have not hit \"Complete purchase\" to finalize the order. You can check to see if this is the case by visiting the Audible site and going to your Purchase history within your account to see if an order was declined. View purchase history to learn step by step how to do this.\n\n## Update your app\n\nIf you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh.\n\nNote: An update will only display if there's one available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n\nUpdate the iOS app\n\n  1. Open the App Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Find the Audible app.\n  4. Select Update.\n\nNote: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\nUpdate the Android app\n\n  1. Open the Google Play Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Select My apps & games.\n  4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\n  5. Select Update.\n\n## Check if the title has been shared (Kids Profile users only)\n\nContent must be shared by the adult account holder to appear in a Kids Profile. See Share with a Kids Profile to learn more.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen with Meta AI glasses (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-on-your-meta-device?language=en_CA)\nciteturn763search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: last week;   * Playing Audible without specifying a title will play whatever title’s already in the player. ... For more details on how to control playback or download titles to your Audible Library from your Meta device, please visit the Meta Help Center. ...   * Thumb swipe up/down to navigate/search for Audible app\n\n## Listen with Meta AI glasses\n\n  * Apr 10, 2026\n\nAnswer\n\nYou can control the Audible app hands-free with Meta AI Glasses voice commands. This includes playing and pausing your audiobook, bookmarking a spot, and searching for specific titles that are available to you.\nTo use Meta AI glasses with Audible, you must have the Audible and the Meta AI apps installed on your phone.\nNote:\n\n  * Playing Audible without specifying a title will play whatever title’s already in the player.\n  * Searching for podcasts isn’t supported at the moment\n  * Only titles you own or have access to with membership or that are in your Library are playable using Meta AI glasses.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * How do I pair my Meta AI glasses to Audible?\n  * What are the voice commands for Audible on my Meta AI glasses?\n  * What touch pad controls are available for Audible on my Meta AI glasses?\n  * How do I listen to Audible on my Meta Ray Ban Display AI glasses?\n  * How do I disconnect Audible from my Meta AI glasses?\n| \"Hey Meta, play Audible.\"\n\"Hey Meta, resume Audible.\"\n\"Hey Meta, continue my audiobook.\"\nPlay a specific audiobook in your Library.  | \"Hey Meta, play Animal Farm.\"\n\"Hey Meta, play my audiobook on Audible.\"\nSkip chapters in your audiobook  | \"Hey Meta, previous chapter\"\n\"Hey Meta, next chapter\"\nPause your audiobook  | \"Hey Meta, pause.\"\nGo back or skip forward  | \"Hey Meta, jump forward\"\n\"Hey Meta, jump back\"\nBookmark a spot  | \"Hey Meta, bookmark this\"\n\"Hey Meta, add a bookmark on Audible\"\n\n## What touch pad controls are available for Audible on my Meta AI glasses?\n\nYou can use the following gestures on your Meta AI glasses touchpad to control playback on Audible. The touchpad is located along the side of the right glasses arm.\n\n  * Tap the touchpad once to pause/resume.\n  * Double tap to jump forward.\n  * Triple tap jump back.\n  * Forward swipe to turn volume up.\n  * Back swipe to turn volume down.\n\n## How do I listen to Audible on my Meta Ray Ban Display AI glasses?\n\nThe Meta Ray-Ban Display glasses feature advanced gesture controls through a Meta neural band that reads hand movements. Using these gestures, you can access your Audible title, play/pause, jump forward and back, and adjust the volume.\nThe glasses can read the following gestures:\n\n  * Thumb swipe up/down to navigate/search for Audible app\n  * Tap thumb to index finger to select Audible app\n  * Double thumb tap to activate \"Hey Meta...\" voice command\n  * Middle finger hold to open the app grid\n  * Rotate dial in the air to adjust volume up and down\n\n## How do I disconnect Audible from my Meta AI glasses?\n\nYou can disconnect the Audible app from your Meta AI glasses anytime in your Meta AI app settings. When disconnecting, the Audible app may briefly open while its unpairing.\n\nNote: If disconnecting through your Meta AI app doesn’t work, you can try uninstalling and reinstalling the Audible app.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApp keeps crashing (https://help.audible.com/s/article/app-keeps-crashing?language=en_US)\nciteturn763search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player. ... Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\n## App keeps crashing\n\nThere are a few troubleshooting methods to try if the Audible app is consistently crashing (closing immediately after opening) or is slowly loading information.\n\n## Force quit the app\n\n  1. Press the home button twice or swipe up from the bottom of your screen.\n  2. Close the Audible app.\n  3. Reopen the Audible app.\n\nIf the issue continues, you may need to update or reinstall your Audible app.\n\n## Update the app\n\nOccasionally, app features and functions may stop working because the app hasn't been updated to the latest version.\n\nNote: An update will only display if there's an update available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n\n### Update the iOS app\n\n  1. Open the App Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Find and select the Audible app.\n  4. Select Update.\n  5. Select Open to view the latest version of the Audible app.\n\nNote: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\n### Update the Android app\n\n  1. Open the Google Play Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Select My apps & games.\n  4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\n  5. Select Update.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMissing title issues (https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-is-missing?language=en_US)\nciteturn763search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; In this article: ... If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player. ... Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\n## Refresh your Library\n\nYou can refresh your Library by swiping down from the top of the screen until you see the spinning circle. (That means it's refreshing.)\n\nIf a swipe-to-refresh doesn't work, you can do a manual refresh:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Profile.\n  3. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  4. Select Library.\n  5. Select Refresh Library.\n\nNote: If you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh. See the \"Update your app\" section below if refreshing doesn't resolve the issue.\n\n## Check your marketplace\n\nYou may be signed in to the wrong Audible marketplace. If that's the case, none of your titles will be available to listen to. Sign out and then sign in to the Audible marketplace where you made your purchases.\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Profile.\n  3. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  4. Scroll down and select Sign Out twice.\n  5. Select Sign In once and you'll be brought to the welcome screen.\n\n  1. Open the Audible app. \n\n  2. Search for the title you are looking for. \n\n  3. Select In your library from the suggestions that appear to find titles you own. \n\nUse this option to find titles that you own and are no longer available in the Audible catalog. \n\n## Check your purchase history on the Audible site\n\nYou can check your recent purchase by going to your Purchase history on the Audible site within your account.\n\nYour default payment method may not have gone through—or you may have not hit \"Complete purchase\" to finalize the order. You can check to see if this is the case by visiting the Audible site and going to your Purchase history within your account to see if an order was declined. View purchase history to learn step by step how to do this.\n\n## Update your app\n\nIf you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh.\n\nNote: An update will only display if there's one available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n\nUpdate the iOS app\n\n  1. Open the App Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Find the Audible app.\n  4. Select Update.\n\nNote: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\nUpdate the Android app\n\n  1. Open the Google Play Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Select My apps & games.\n  4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\n  5. Select Update.\n\nCheck if the title has been shared (Kids Profile users only)\n\nContent must be shared by the adult account holder to appear in a Kids Profile. See Share with a Kids Profile to learn more.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about Audible Plus (https://help.audible.com/s/article/learn-about-audible-plus?language=en_US)\nciteturn763search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month;   * Ways to listen: You can enjoy Audible content through the mobile app or online player. ... In this article: ... Swipe down to \"More from your membership.\"\n\nAudible Plus Membership Plans Plans & benefits\n\n## Learn about Audible Plus\n\n  * Sep 3, 2026\n\nTitle\n\nLearn about Audible Plus\n\nURL Name\n\nlearn-about-audible-plus\n\nAnswer\n\nOur Audible Plus membership lets you stream or download thousands of titles from the included catalog. It includes access to podcasts, audiobooks, and Audible Originals. If you enjoy podcasts and short-form content, you might enjoy this plan.\n\nWith an Audible Plus monthly membership, you will have access to:\n\n  * Finding and playing titles: It's easy to browse through audiobooks, podcasts, and Originals in the Audible library. You can stream all you want from the included catalog. Want to buy individual titles? You can do that too, whether you're a member or not.\n  * Ways to listen: You can enjoy Audible content through the mobile app or online player. On the app, you can download your favorite titles to listen offline.\n  * Cancellation and pausing: You can cancel your plan anytime. Remember that if you cancel, you'll lose access to the included catalog and any unused credits.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * How do I sign up for the Audible Plus membership?\n  * How do I find titles in the included catalog?\n  * What membership plans does Audible offer?\n  * Can I listen to Audible titles with the Amazon Prime subscription?\n\n## How do I sign up for the Audible Plus membership?\n\nAs of March 3, 2026, new members cannot sign up for Audible Plus. If you're already an Audible Plus member, you can keep your plan. The Audible Premium and Audible Standard are still available for new members.\n\n## How do I find titles in the included catalog?\n\nYou can find included titles in your membership from the app or website.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to Discover.\n  3. Swipe down to \"More from your membership.\"\n  4. Select Included.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Included.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Select the main menu.\n  2. Select Explore Audible.\n  3. Select Plus Catalog.\n\n## What membership plans does Audible offer?\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage your Library (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-library?language=en_US&msockid=22cb8dbf3a966c8115809bc83be16dff)\nciteturn763search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; In this article: ... Simply swipe left on the screen to view them all. ... Note: If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Library.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select Library in the site navigation.\n\n## How can I use my Library?\n\nIn the app\n\nThere are several ways you can view and sort titles in your in-app Library. At the very top of the screen, you'll find your main sections—Audiobooks, Podcasts, Wish List, Lists, Authors, Series, and Genres. Simply swipe left on the screen to view them all.\n\nYour in-app Library also features filters, which allow you to see all of your titles at once or only those that are Not started, In progress, Downloaded, and Finished.\n\n### Use the In your library filter in catalog search\n\nWhen searching in the Audible app, you can use the In your library filter to narrow search results to titles in your Library only.\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Search for the title you are looking for.\n  3. Select In your library from the suggestions that appear to find titles you own.\n\nUse this option to find titles that you own and are no longer available in the Audible catalog.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApp keeps crashing (https://help.audible.com/s/article/app-keeps-crashing?nocache=https%3A%2F%2Fhelp.audible.com%2Fs%2Farticle%2Fapp-keeps-crashing%3Flanguage%3Den_US)\nciteturn763search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; In this article: ... If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player. ... Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\n## App keeps crashing\n\n  * Aug 27, 2026\n\nAnswer\n\nThere are a few troubleshooting methods to try if the Audible app is consistently crashing (closing immediately after opening) or is slowly loading information.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * Force quit the app\n  * Update the app\n  * Clear app data and cache on Android\n  * Re-install the app\n  * Temporary fixes\n\n## Force quit the app\n\n  1. Press the home button twice or swipe up from the bottom of your screen.\n  2. Close the Audible app.\n  3. Reopen the Audible app.\n\nIf the issue continues, you may need to update or reinstall your Audible app.\n\n## Update the app\n\nOccasionally, app features and functions may stop working because the app hasn't been updated to the latest version.\n\nNote: An update will only display if there's an update available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCan’t sign in or out (https://help.audible.com/s/article/can-t-sign-in-or-out?language=it)\nciteturn763search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.2 years ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Note: If you don’t see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates. ... If you’re using an older device that doesn’t support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\n\n## Can’t sign in or out\n\nThere are a few reasons you may be having trouble signing in to your account. We’ve provided potential reasons for that and troubleshooting steps to perform.\n\n## Check that your sign-in credentials are correct\n\nPasswords are case-sensitive and being off by a single letter will affect your ability to sign in.\nIf you believe you’re entering the correct username and password and still can’t sign in, we recommend resetting your password by visiting the password assistance page on Amazon. \nIf you’ve recently signed out of the app, you might receive a generic error message when you attempt to sign in again. The error message will trigger an email with a one-time password. Please use the one-time password to sign in and update your password to something new.\nNote: This password will only be valid for 10 minutes. The email will come from Amazon with no reference to Audible. \n\n## Check your app version\n\n### Update the iOS app\n\n  1. Open the App Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Find the Audible app.\n  4. Select Update.\n\nNote: If you don’t see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n  \n\n### Update the Android app\n\n  1. Open the Google Play Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Select My apps & games.\n\nFind the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\nNote: An update will only display if there’s one available to download. If you’re using an older device that doesn’t support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAudio quality issues (https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality?nocache=https%3A%2F%2Fhelp.audible.com%2Fs%2Farticle%2Ftitle-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality%3Flanguage%3Den_US)\nciteturn763search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; In this article, you'll find troubleshooting steps for general playback issues by device type. ... Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates. ... Try listening to the title using our Cloud Player or another Audible-ready device to see if the issue continues. ... To remove a teen profile from your Amazon Family, please visit Amazon's Help Center.\n\n## Audio quality issues\n\n  * Sep 9, 2026\n  * Knowledge\n\nTitle\n\nAudio quality issues\n\nURL Name\n\ntitle-won-t-play-has-poor-audio-quality\n\nAnswer\n\nIn this article, you'll find troubleshooting steps for general playback issues by device type.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * Playback issues in the app\n  * Playback issues on your Samsung or Pixel device\n  * How to fix playback issues on Alexa\n  * Playback issues on Fire Tablet\n  * Playback issues on Fire TV\n  * Playback issues on Cloud Player\n\n## Playback issues in the app\n\nUpdate app\n\nIf your title won't play, you may have to update your Audible app.\n\nTo update the Audible app on iOS:\n\n  1. Open the App Store.\n  2. Select your profile icon.\n  3. Find and select the Audible app.\n  4. Select Update.\n  5. Select Open to view the latest version of the Audible app.\n\nNote: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\n\nTo update the Audible app on Android:\n\n  1. \nForce stop the app\n\nIf your title won't play at all, you may have to force stop your Audible app.\n\n  1. Drag down from the top of the screen and tap the Settings gear icon followed by Apps & Games.\n  2. Tap Manage All Applications followed by Audible Store.\n  3. Tap Force Stop followed by OK.\n\nUpdate your device\n\n  1. Go to the Settings gear icon on your Tablet home page.\n  2. Scroll down to Device Options.\n  3. Select System Updates and select Update.\n\n## Playback issues on Fire TV\n\n  * Check your device's internet connection.\n  * Make sure you're signed in to the correct account.\n  * If your username for Audible isn't the same for Amazon, combine your Amazon and Audible accounts.\n  * Go to your Purchase History page to check that the title you're trying to listen to has a date listed under the Purchased column.\n  * If you use the Fire TV Remote app on your phone, make sure the app is updated to the latest version.\n\n## Playback issues on Cloud Player\n\nIf you are experiencing playback issues, something could have happened with your saved browser history that is causing the Cloud Player to not pop up.\n"
